      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-05-26_WidnesExaminer_art0011" n="art0011">
        <head>GOLF.</head>
        <p>GOLF.</p>
        <p>LOCAL PLAYERS IN PARLIAMENTARY HANDiCAP.— In the Parliamentary tournament, on Saturday, at Littleton-on-See, Kent, in the first round Mr. C. D. Schwann beat Mr. J. F. L. Brunner by one hole, Mr. T. Long heat Lord Newton by 3 and I, and Mr. A. H. Crosfield had a walk-over. In the second round Mr. L. Atherley Jones beat Sir .1. Brunner by 3 and 2, and Mr. Crosfield beat Mr. Wills by 6 and 4. FLIXTON V. MERSEY (FKNKETII).-At Flixton on Saturday. Scores :</p>
        <p>MERSEY. W. Heyes 0 F. %V. Gilbert D. T. Delany 1 C. R Adamson (captain) 0 .1. Spink - 1 J. M. Murray A. B. Barnes S. Kneale 0 G. G. Ainsworth 0 A. V. Slater 1 R. N. Foster 0 H. S. Holmes 1 R. H. Pearson 0 0. W. Heald W. H. Eyre (captain) ... 1 F. Jnynson T. Lightfoot W. Bolton T. H. Bissel</p>
        <p>F L 1 XTON.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-05-26_WidnesExaminer_art0012" n="art0012">
        <p>.--.i.,.....</p>
        <p>At Yarmouth on Tuesday an Auctioneer's clerk went to the workshop of Mr. James' Gallant, builder, and discovered him hanging lifeless from a beam. The deceased had filed his petition on Saturday, and a bankruptcy notice served upon him was found in his pocket.</p>
