      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-05-26_WidnesExaminer_art0120" n="art0120">
        <head>Death of Mr. R. Evans.</head>
        <p>Death of Mr. R. Evans.</p>
        <p>--- -- Many of our readers will regret to hear of the death of Mr. R. Evans, 41, Thewlis-street, who passed away suddenly on Thursday morning of last week. The deceased gentleman, who was 63 years of age, retired to rest on Wednesday night apparently in his usual health. Early the following morning he com- plained of fueling very unwell and Dr. Braid° was sent for. Onk his arrival, however, he found that death had taken place, the cause being heart failure. Mr. Evans was an accomplished musician and was well-known and highly esteemed in musical circles in Warrington and neighbourhood. He had acted as organist at Holy Trinity Church Warrington, and Walton Parish Church, filling both positions with great ability. Recently he had taken occasional duty at local churches. He was of a kindly and unassuming disposition, and his death, coming so unexpectedly, will occasion genuine regret to a wide circle of friends. lhe funeral took place very quietly at the Csmetery on Monday afternoon. There were numerous beautiful floral tributss, including one from Holy Trinity Church choir.</p>
      </div>
