        <p>14.,,,,,i- --,--"—.. "' '-4. '‘ ' ."' ' .t",‘""'''''',, 4.4,4,4 tAO 0 '•:,,t ' .'lt 4 41,1:1:1' 454 oldoof oiro if r, I----= , • i 7 Moonlight Runs. it is surprising that more is not heard nowadays of moonlight fixtures. Years ago these rides, often extending into the small hours, were highly popular among the clubs. A supper was arranged for at some favourite resort, about twenty miles from headquarters. and the return journey made in the brilliant light of a full moon. Familiar scenery, viewed under these conditions, reveals new and unsuspected charms. Weird shadows are flung athwart the highway by trees and telegraph poles, while the hills seem to have lost their terrors._ An almost magical tranquillity enwraps the country. side, and little tiaffic of any sort ,is encountered.</p>
